OBJECTIVE
Identify a data-intensive problem from your current work environment and design a Big Data solution using the tools and techniques learned in this course. This demonstrates your ability to translate domain knowledge into technical solutions.
REQUIREMENTS
Problem Identification (3 Marks)
Clearly describe the business context and domain
Identify the specific data problem/challenge
Explain why this is a "Big Data" problem (volume, velocity, variety)
Define the objectives and expected outcomes

Solution Design (4 Marks)
Data sourcing strategy (what data, from where, format)
Architecture design using Hadoop ecosystem tools
Detailed implementation plan covering:
Data ingestion approach
Processing workflow (which tools for which tasks)
Storage strategy
Analysis methodology


Proof of Concept (3 Marks)
Implement a small but meaningful part of your solution
Use at least 3 different Hadoop tools from the course
Demonstrate working prototype with sample data
Show preliminary results/insights
DELIVERABLES
Project Proposal Document (2-3 pages) covering:
Problem statement and business context
Data landscape description
Solution architecture diagram
Implementation timeline

Technical Implementation including:
Code/scripts for the proof of concept
Sample dataset used for testing
Screenshots of execution and results

Final Presentation (5-7 slides) covering:
Problem significance
Proposed solution
Proof of concept demonstration
Business impact and future scope
